          "message": "ci(formal): kani + miri nightly lanes produce a real green verdict — split known-timeout debt from a genuine regression [FABLE-5] (#1884)\n\n* ci(formal): let the kani + miri nightly lanes produce a real green verdict — separate known-timeout debt from a genuine regression [FABLE-5]\n\nBoth formal lanes had gone >48h with no successful verdict (#1788 kani, #1789 miri),\ntripping formal-alarm.yml. Root cause (both): the workflow-run conclusion mixes the\nHEALTHY, genuinely-passing proofs/tests with KNOWN, BEAD-TRACKED cost debt, so a single\nalways-red debt item poisons the whole run's conclusion forever — the healthy core can\nnever register a green verdict and the no-verdict alarm fires perpetually.\n\n  * kani: 3 of 5 suites pass every night (25 substrate order-law proofs + 5 dict\n    id-partition proofs + 6 engine reducer proofs). The 2 mmap-validator TOTALITY suites\n    exceed the 20m per-harness CBMC budget and TIMEOUT every night — bounding tracked by\n    sq-og8u8 (not yet done). Fix: mark those two suites `debt: true`; a pure TIMEOUT there\n    is recorded LOUDLY (step summary + ::warning::) but is NON-FATAL, while a real Kani\n    counterexample/build error STILL reds the job. Healthy suites determine the verdict.\n\n  * miri: the UB lane's purpose (detect aliasing/provenance/data-race UB) is intact — but\n    ~20 heavy end-to-end loader tests genuinely blow the per-test cap under Miri's ~100x\n    slowdown (a COST problem tracked by sq-0s15k). `cargo miri nextest` exits 100 for a\n    TIMEOUT and a real UB FAILURE alike, so the raw exit made the whole workflow red every\n    night on cost debt. Fix: emit nextest's libtest-json-plus events to a file and let the\n    new scripts/miri_classify_verdict.py split TIMEOUT (reason \"time limit exceeded\";\n    known debt, non-fatal) from a GENUINE failure (real UB abort/assertion; always fatal).\n    A healthy night now produces a real green UB verdict; a single genuine UB regression\n    still reds the shard + workflow + re-fires the alarm. UB guarantee unchanged.\n\nNo proof deleted, no bound lowered, no gate weakened: the debt stays LOUD + under standing\npressure (sq-og8u8, sq-0s15k) and a genuine regression still reds the lane. Flip `debt`\noff / drop the classifier's timeout tolerance the instant those beads land.\n\nVerified: kani.yml/miri.yml valid YAML + actionlint clean; miri_classify_verdict self-test\n+ formal_lane_alarm self-test + check-fv-manifest drift gate all green; end-to-end nextest\nlibtest-json-plus classification reproduced locally (timeout-only => exit 0; real failure\n=> exit 1).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(formal): wire the Miri verdict classifier's self-test into the ci-scripts PR gate + a fast miri.yml guard [FABLE-5]\n\nMatch the repo convention (every CI-helper carries a hermetic --self-test enforced on\nevery PR): scripts/miri_classify_verdict.py could silently turn the UB lane green if it\nregressed, so run its self-test in docs-quality.yml's ci-scripts leg (caught on every PR\ntouching it) and as a fast guard step at the top of the miri job (before the ~2h shard\nrun) so a broken classifier reds the shard immediately instead of mis-judging the run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(formal): harden the Miri verdict classifier — an empty event stream is FATAL, not a clean pass [FABLE-5]\n\nSilence must not look like green at the shard level either: if nextest emits no ok/failed/\ntimeout events (build break / miri sysroot failure / crash before emitting), the classifier\nnow reds the shard instead of reporting all-pass. Added a self-test case exercising the\nempty-stream fatal path + a real-pass path end-to-end through main().\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <jw896977@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
