          "message": "fix(engine): builtin memoize + REGEX/REPLACE memo + RAND PRNG + NOW() query-constancy — O(n²) Turtle-parse hang fix (sq-98w7z.1) (#1901)\n\n* perf(engine): REGEX/REPLACE compile memo + RAND thread-local PRNG + NOW() query-constancy fix (sq-98w7z.1) [FABLE-5]\n\nSalvaged from a prior agent's uncommitted worktree, judged coherent and kept:\n- regex_cache: per-thread capped (64) memo {(pattern,flags) -> Option<Rc<Regex>>};\n  compile failures memoised (invalid pattern stays a per-row type error).\n- rand_unit: per-thread splitmix64 seeded once from OS entropy replaces the\n  per-row uuid-v4 OS draw behind RAND().\n- query_now: outermost-wins execution scope pinned in eval_modified so every\n  NOW() in one execution (rows, rayon workers, EXISTS re-entry, sub-selects)\n  returns the same instant (SPARQL 1.1 section 17.4.5.1), cleared on outermost\n  drop so the next execution re-samples; worker_install at every parallel\n  expression-eval site + a cfg(test) unscoped-fallback probe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sparq-core): O(n²) Turtle terminator scan hang + feature-OFF test gating (sq-98w7z.1) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nRoot cause of the 19-min unit-test hang (finishing sq-98w7z.1). The builtin-memo\nNOW-constancy test `now_parallel_rows_single_instant_no_fallback` was the first to\nbuild a >50k-row QUOTE-FREE Turtle document and hand it to the parallel parser. The\nmemoize/NOW/regex code is innocent — the hang is a pre-existing latent O(n²) in the\nparallel Turtle splitter.\n\n`next_terminator` ran TWO full-tail `memchr3` scans per state-change byte\n(`. < #` and `\" ' \\`) and took `x.min(y)`. On a body with no string literals or\nPN_LOCAL escapes the second scan found nothing and re-walked the ENTIRE remaining\nbuffer once per statement, making the splitter O(statement·tail) ⇒ whole-parse O(n²).\nMeasured on the work box (non-canonical): 10k rows = 150 s, 55k ≈ hours.\n\nFix: bound the second `memchr3` to the window BEFORE the first `. < #` — behaviour is\nidentical (proved by the existing `next_terminator_memchr_matches_scalar` oracle over\nevery start offset), each byte is now scanned at most once, restoring O(n). 10k rows:\n150 s → 0.086 s; the 55k NOW test that hung now runs in 0.42 s; the full `builtin_memo`\nsuite completes in 1.22 s.\n\nAlso fixes a feature-OFF break the memoize work introduced: `now_parallel_*` referenced\n`parallel`-gated `PAR_THRESHOLD` and `names_graph` had only `regex`-gated callers, both\ndead/unresolved under `--no-default-features` (would have failed the CI feature-OFF leg).\nGated both.\n\nTests: `parallel_turtle_terminator_scan_is_linear_not_quadratic` (hard 20 s wall-clock\nceiling — non-vacuous: pre-fix ≈600 s, fixed <1 s) + two quote-free differential cases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(bench): feature-OFF wasm declaration for PR #1901 (sq-98w7z.1) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThe always-compiled next_terminator O(n²) fix moves feature-OFF sparq-wasm bytes.\nMeasured (work-box reproduction of the vectorized-feature-off leg2, base 6ec1a2da3 vs\nhead, release-wasm, default features): SIZE +0 bytes (1580701 -> 1580701, +0.0000%,\ninside the ±2% band). wasm-tools objdump: CODE section byte-identical (same 1476218 B,\n2495 fns), DATA section same size (69459 B) with an identical string set (0 added /\n0 removed); only 279 bytes differ, all in data, all a uniform &str-pointer emission-order\nshift. No parser/memoize symbol leaks. Leg2-dynamic accepts the declaration (verified,\nexit 0). No perf-baseline.json change (0-byte delta).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <jw896977@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
